# Notice

## Integrated engines

Downloader engine code migrated from the project author's own earlier tools is
embedded in the engine packages, licensed under the same [LICENSE](LICENSE)
(MIT):

- `src/dler_kun/engines/85xo/xo_dler/` — 85xo crawler/downloader (from `vendor/85xo/xo_dler`)
- `src/dler_kun/engines/gofile/gofile_dl/` — GoFile downloader (from `vendor/gofile/gofile_dl`)

## Vendored tools

- `src/dler_kun/vendor/twimg/download_twitter_media.py` — twitter/tweetfile
  media downloader (invoked as a subprocess; still vendored)

No third-party code is embedded; these are the author's own implementations.

## External tools

dler-kun invokes the following as separate executables (never bundled or
linked):

- **ffmpeg** (LGPL/GPL) — used to mux HLS segments into MP4 (`mixixxx` engine).
  Install from your OS package manager or https://ffmpeg.org.
- **Google Chrome / Microsoft Edge** — used headlessly to fetch
  TLS-fingerprint-bound HLS (`mixixxx` engine). Your own browser install.

## Dependencies

Runtime dependencies (`requests`, `cryptography`, `aiohttp`, `aiohttp-socks`,
`rich`) retain their respective licenses (MIT / Apache-2.0).
